  "evidence": "A: Massive care expansions (e.g., NHS revenue rising £8bn to £28bn by 2030; free personal care; +£40/week to UC, end sanctions; free school meals for all children); liberal migration measures (end hostile environment/NRPF, safe routes, right to work, free NHS for visa holders, voting rights for residents); justice/policing changes that roll back state authority (repeal protest‑curbing laws; end routine stop‑and‑search/facial recognition; presumption against short custodial sentences; decriminalise sex work); identity changes (self‑ID for trans people); defence/international shifts (sign UN nuclear ban, cancel Trident, NATO ‘no first use’, aim to rejoin EU).\nB: Care provisions (NHS spending to rise above inflation; recruit 92,000 nurses/28,000 doctors; expand mental health access; 30 hours free childcare from 9 months); strong authority/loyalty signals (8,000 more neighbourhood police; tougher sentences; four new prisons; new protest controls; counter‑extremism; mandatory National Service; defence spending to 2.5% of GDP; Veterans’ Bill); migration control (annual legal cap that falls each year; higher salary thresholds; Rwanda removals); proportionality cues in welfare (tighter work capability assessments; stronger sanctions; fraud bill); sanctity‑coded measures (Tobacco and Vapes Bill; single‑sex accommodation rights; implement Cass Review).",
